# AI triggers (SuperApp curriculum)

When the user uses a **trigger phrase**, run the matching script from `scripts/ops/` or `prompts/triggers/` — do not improvise deploy commands.

| Phrase | Script |
|--------|--------|
| create new app | `node scripts/ops/new-app.mjs` |
| bootstrap github | `bash scripts/ops/github-bootstrap.sh --confirm` |
| check the stack | `bash scripts/ops/stack-check.sh` |
| run the stack | `bash scripts/ops/stack-run.sh` |
| pull latest | `bash scripts/ops/git-pull.sh` |
| push to github | `bash scripts/ops/git-push.sh` |
| setup hosting | `bash scripts/ops/hosting-setup.sh --host <id>` |
| deploy staging | `deploy-staging.sh --confirm` only if user explicitly asked |
| deploy production | `deploy-prod.sh --confirm` only if user explicitly asked |

Rules:
- GitHub push is not a live deploy.
- Never pass `--confirm` for staging/prod unless the user clearly requested that environment.
- Use `projects/<slug>/` paths, not machine-specific home directories.
- Run `scripts/leak-scan.sh` before public GitHub push.

Index: `prompts/triggers/INDEX.md`
